                ORDER GRANTING MOTION TO FILE TESTIMONY OUT OF TIME

            THIS MATTER comes before Keven Gedko and Nicholas Rossi, hearing examiners for

the New Mexico Public Regulation Commission (“Commission”), upon Stephen Fischmann’s

Motion to File Testimony Out of Time (“Motion”), filed on October 27, 2026. Being duly

informed, the Hearing Examiners FIND and CONCLUDE:

            1.     The Order Establishing Revised Procedural Schedule and Addressing Outstanding

Motions established October 23, 2026, as the deadline for the filing of intervenors’ direct

testimony.1

            2.     On October 27, 2026, Stephen Fischmann filed the Motion, which explains that Mr.

Fischmann and his witnesses missed the deadline for the filing of direct testimony because of

miscommunication over who would make the filing on the PRCe360 system.2

            3.     The Motion asserts that no party is prejudiced by the Motion, and notes that no

parties oppose the Motion.3

            4.     The Motion requests the Commission allow Mr. Fischmann to file the testimony of

Joel Hornstein and Mark Ellis, on their behalf, out of time.4




1
